Manage the per-user macOS background adapter

Usage:
  mcp-runtime adapter service [command]

Available Commands:
  install     Install or update the LaunchAgent and start at login
  logs        Show bounded, redacted diagnostic events as JSON
  reconnect   Reload validated profiles and reconnect without extending consent
  restart     Drain and restart the user service
  run         Run the protected daemon in the foreground
  start       Start the installed user service
  status      Show measured daemon and profile state as JSON
  stop        Stop the user service until started or next login
  uninstall   Stop and remove the LaunchAgent; preserve profiles by default

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for service

Global Flags:
      --debug              Enable debug mode with structured error logging
      --state-dir string   Owner-only adapter state directory (default "~/.mcpruntime/adapter")

Use "mcp-runtime adapter service [command] --help" for more information about a command.
